      "attack_diagnosis": "Myasthenia Gravis. The combination of ocular symptoms (diplopia worsening with gaze), ptosis (implied by difficulty looking up/down), proximal muscle weakness, fatigability that improves with rest, and positive AChR antibodies with decreased response on repetitive nerve stimulation is diagnostic. REQUEST IMAGES: Chest CT scan to evaluate for thymoma.",
